	'ke444c73f' => 'Our operational calendar balances clear deadlines across both client and bureau responsibilities. On the 20th, raw attendance data is finalized by the employer. Across the 21st and 22nd, Getsuji Payroll performs gross-to-net calculations alongside our mandatory two-person check on every run. On the 23rd, the business owner approves the wage ledger. On the 25th, employees receive their net salaries and electronic payslips. Finally, on the last working day, Pieter Claes completes mandatory social security filings. This five-stage timetable ensures every party knows their role well in advance.',
